    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI Summarization\n\nUses OpenRouter's free model router.\n\nThe prompt requires a strict JSON schema because the\nReact frontend consumes the response programmatically.\n\nDo not remove `response_format`.",
        "height": 304,
        "width": 304
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        624,
        288
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "619798e7-e971-412e-8f2d-0ec97a5a684b",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# BoilDocs — Documentation Summarizer\n\nTurns technical documentation into structured developer notes.\n\n## Flow\n\n1. Receive a documentation URL or pasted text.\n2. Fetch the documentation when a URL is provided.\n3. Clean the HTML into readable text.\n4. Send the content to an OpenRouter free model.\n5. Force a predictable JSON response.\n6. Validate the generated structure.\n7. Return the result to the React frontend.\n\n## External Services\n\n- OpenRouter — LLM inference\n- Documentation URL — source content\n\n## Security\n\n- Never commit API credentials.\n- OpenRouter credentials are stored in n8n.\n- Webhook should be protected before production use.\n\n## Frontend Contract\n\nPOST /webhook/boildocs\n\nInput:\n- sourceType: `url` | `text`\n- source: string\n\nOutput:\n- title\n- oneLiner\n- concepts\n- sections\n- quickStart\n- caveats\n\n## Developed and maintained by https://github.com/supersver\n\n## Checkout more workflows at https://github.com/supersver/n8n-workflows",
        "height": 1200,
        "width": 512
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
